<title>DENMARK: 600 Danish trucks seek to block German border.</title>
<headline>600 Danish trucks seek to block German border.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>About 600 Danish truckers attempted to disrupt traffic on the motorway linking Denmark and Germany on Monday in a protest over taxes, but were having little impact, police said.</p>
<p>The trucks were trying to blockade the Padborg customs area at the Danish-German frontier in south Jutland.</p>
<p>&quot;The strike action is a tax protest. Some 500-600 Danish trucks are staging a blockade, but only the actual customs area at the Padborg checkpoint is affected,&quot; a police spokesman said. &quot;The bulk of the traffic between the two countries is flowing normally along the motorway.&quot;</p>
<p>He said negotiations were underway between truck drivers and the Danish tax ministry to end the action.</p>
</text>
